    "created_at": "2019-04-24T18:38:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-04-24T18:38:47Z",
    "body": "I don't know about the accessibility requirements but given that a video needs to be able to play audio, it seems indeed logical that <video> should be able to play audio-only files. FWIW, all browsers I know of do this. They usually even go out of their way to change the native controls to make them look an audio player.\r\n\r\nIn short, I'm fine with adding this but I would drop the accessibility reasons.",
